                                                                                "take":  "Santoli is highlighting a structural fragility that deserves more attention than it typically gets: when index leadership concentrates back into a handful of mega-caps to push records, the market\u0027s apparent health is narrower than the headline number implies. A bull market that needs Big Tech to carry it again is a bull market that has not broadened out, and lack of breadth is one of the more reliable leading indicators of eventual index vulnerability. The practical implication: don\u0027t mistake an S\u0026P 500 record for a healthy market-wide rally. Investors in equal-weight or small-cap strategies are likely still in a different, more frustrating market than the cap-weight index suggests.",
